sequenceDiagram
    participant ClientA as Client A
    participant ClientB as Client B
    participant Socket as socket.js
    participant Map as connectedUsers Map
    participant REST as REST API messageRoutes.js
    participant DB as MongoDB

    Note over ClientA,Socket: Connect - Chat.jsx opens one socket per session on mount<br/>io(ENDPOINT, { auth: { user: userInfo } })
    ClientA->>Socket: io connect with auth user, triggers connection event
    Socket->>Socket: user = socket.handshake.auth.user, no JWT check<br/>(unverified - a deliberate simplification, see LECTURE.md)

    Note over ClientA,Map: Groups double as Socket.IO rooms - joining a group's<br/>chat = socket.join(groupId). This is how members of<br/>the same group become "interconnected": the server<br/>fans out events only to sockets that joined that room.
    ClientA->>Socket: emit join room with groupId
    Socket->>Socket: socket.join(groupId)
    Socket->>Map: connectedUsers.set socket.id, user and room
    Socket-->>ClientA: emit users in room, to whole room
    Socket-->>ClientB: emit users in room, to whole room
    Socket-->>ClientB: emit notification type USER_JOINED

    ClientA->>Socket: emit typing with groupId and username
    Socket-->>ClientB: emit user typing with username
    Note over Socket,ClientB: Typing state is ephemeral - broadcast only,<br/>never written to the DB or the presence Map

    ClientA->>Socket: emit stop typing with groupId
    Socket-->>ClientB: emit user stop typing with username

    Note over ClientA,DB: Sending a message is two separate client calls -<br/>ChatArea.jsx's sendMessage() does both, in order.<br/>See 07-send-message.mmd for the REST leg in detail.
    ClientA->>REST: 1. POST /api/messages { content, groupId }, Bearer token
    REST->>DB: Message.create + populate sender
    DB-->>REST: populatedMessage
    REST-->>ClientA: 200 populatedMessage - this is the source of truth
    ClientA->>Socket: 2. emit new message with populatedMessage, groupId
    Socket-->>ClientB: emit message received, relay only, no DB write
    Note over Socket: socket.to(groupId) excludes the sender - ClientA already<br/>has the message from the REST response, so it appends<br/>it locally instead of waiting for this echo

    ClientA->>Socket: emit leave room with groupId
    Socket->>Socket: socket.leave(groupId)
    Socket->>Map: connectedUsers.delete socket.id
    Socket-->>ClientB: emit user left with user id

    Note over ClientA,Socket: On disconnect event, tab close or network drop -<br/>same cleanup as an explicit leave room
    Socket->>Map: lookup and delete connectedUsers entry
    Socket-->>ClientB: emit user left with user id

    Note over Map: connectedUsers is an in-memory Map local to this<br/>server process. Presence resets on restart and would<br/>need a shared store (e.g. Redis) to scale beyond one instance.
